# ── 2026-09-17b-ptrmentionland: TWO DEFECTS FOUND BY THE ABUSE DIRECTION OF A CONDEMNED ARM ──
# Both reproduce on the SHIPPED compiler with NO probe installed (build_hash 8f5483d04b7c49ac 43).
# They were found by carrier-varied counter-examples written to price `collect_param_regions_`
# gaining a K::Ptr arm; that arm was MEASURED, REFUTED and NOT landed (it admits two programs
# rustc refuses, E0597 each). These two rows need no arm and are independent of it.
#
# ptr_under_struct_field_region_escape_admitted — CLOSED 2026-09-17h-ptrland, run-verified.
#    `type_is_ha` and `bc_holds_any_ref_type` gained a `Ptr` arm recursing into the pointee, so a
#    raw pointer TO a reference now carries one: `Holder` enters `holds_any_ref`, the by-value
#    parameter is seeded, the summary no longer claims `result<-0 EXACT`, and the program is
#    REFUSED — "'r' does not live long enough … (E0597)", the escaping borrow named rather than the
#    variance accident. Landed as tests/logos/fail/bc_0917h_ptrland_hb_x1_refuse; the TUPLE-field
#    and ARRAY-field carriers, which were unrowed and ran 8 and 6 on the shipped binary, are closed
#    by the SAME change and landed beside it as hb_x2/hb_x3.
#
# refptr_param_eq_compares_outer_ref — `==` on a `&*mut T` PARAMETER compares the OUTER REFERENCE
#    instead of the pointer, so two copies of one pointer compare unequal: exit 1 where rustc gives 0.
#    ⚠ It CORRECTS a recorded claim: round 2026-09-17a saw this only through `&*mut &'a i64`, whose
#    shape is refused on base by an unrelated region defect, and recorded it as "unreachable until
#    the region door opens — doors in series". With no inner reference it is reachable TODAY.
#    Control on the same binary: the direct `p == q` spelling runs 0, correctly.

